%[text] # Quadcopter Drone Model in Simscape
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:../../MainMenu.m)
%[text] Bringing together all the concepts, we can now look at a detailed model of a quadcopter with physical constraints, multiple subsystems (including electrical and thermal modeling), and realistic trajectories. This model is from the [**Quadcopter Drone Model in Simscape**](https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/63580-quadcopter-drone-model-in-simscape) FileExchange entry, and uses a [MATLAB Project](https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/projects.html) to organize all the files.
%[text] To run the Full Quadcopter Model simulation, you can [open the project in MATLAB Online](https://matlab.mathworks.com/open/fileexchange/v1?id=63580&project=Quadcopter_Drone.prj). 
%[text] Alternately, you can download and run the project locally.
ChooseDirName = "QuadcopterDrone"; %[control:editfield:0960]{"position":[17,34]}
URL = "https://github.com/mathworks/Quadcopter-Drone-Model-Simscape.git";
ProjFile = "Quadcopter_Drone.prj";
% Use a local helper function to download the File Exchange directory
DownloadExampleFromFileExchange(ChooseDirName,URL,ProjFile);
  %[control:button:475e]{"position":[1,2]}
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Block diagram of Manuever Controller, Environment, Quadcopter, Scope, and Reference](text:image:2926)
%[text] Explore the model to see the various subsystems:
%[text] - electrical, 
%[text] - mechanical 
%[text] - and maneuver controller.  \
%[text] When running the model, we should be able to see a 3-D visualization of the quadcopter as it delivers a package and returns to its original location. We can see that this model is made up of a number of complex sub-systems, which define how it operates. After looking through the model, please close the model and the project and return to this script.
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_928F02EC] **Further Exercises (Optional)**
%[text] Aside from the Package Delivery Simulation, there are several other exercises included in the Project package. From the top of the Project Shortcuts Toolbar, click on 'Exercise Select' to open and run these.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Screenshot of contents of 'Exercise Select'](text:image:6a34)
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Screenshot of Exercise Selection App showing 5 exercises that can be started by clicking the relevant button](text:image:65d8)
%%
%[text] Reset the project by clicking the Return Here button before continuing:
  %[control:button:8350]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:../../MainMenu.m)
%%
%[text] ## Help us Improve
%[text] [Share your feedback](<matlab: ShareFeedback>) to help us improve this module.
function ReturnHere() %#ok<DEFNU>
curloc = matlab.desktop.editor.getActiveFilename;
if contains(curloc,"Scripts")
    rootdir = extractBefore(curloc,filesep+"Scripts");
elseif contains(curloc,"InstructorResources")
    rootdir = extractBefore(curloc,filesep+"InstructorResources");
else
    error("Unexpected location: " + curloc)
end
cd(rootdir)
end

